WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
He's mingled with witches and done battle&nbsp;
with vampires — it's clear that The Last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.100
Kingdom's Alexander Dreymon has a&nbsp;
knack for spellbinding spectacle.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:13.740
Netflix's ninth-century costume drama The Last&nbsp;
Kingdom was adapted from the successful Saxon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:18.600
Stories series of historical adventure novels&nbsp;
from renowned English author Bernard Cornwell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:24.960
Originally produced by BBC Two in the U.K. and&nbsp;
BBC America in the US, Netflix became the sole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.700
producer of the series from Season 3 onward –&nbsp;
stepping up to foot the show's substantial bill.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.540
The books — and show — follows the&nbsp;
exploits of Uhtred of Bebbanburg,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.800
the dispossessed scion of a noble house in&nbsp;
the ancient English kingdom of Northumbria.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:43.260
The Saxon Stories book series currently sits at&nbsp;
13 entries, with the final installment hitting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:48.420
shelves back in 2020. This proved fortunate&nbsp;
for Netflix, as The Last Kingdom adapted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.861
Cornwell's books at a respectable pace,&nbsp;
chewing up about two novels per season.

00:00:52.861 --> 00:00:54.120
"I gave you glory!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.760
I gave you the freedom to worship your God,&nbsp;
and still you treat me no better than a hound."

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.180
Uhtred is played by Alexander Dreymon — and if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:06.240
you think his handsome visage looks&nbsp;
familiar, there's a very good reason.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:11.640
According to IMDb, Alexander Dreymon was born in&nbsp;
Germany, though he lived for some time in France,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:15.120
and moved to England to study at&nbsp;
the prestigious Drama Centre London,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:20.340
which permanently closed its doors in 2022.&nbsp;
He earned his thespian stripes performing on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:24.600
the stage in both Paris and London before&nbsp;
making the jump to television and film.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.760
Dreymon's first major role on American television&nbsp;
was as a recurring character on the third season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:34.920
of the popular American Horror Story anthology&nbsp;
series. Dreymon played the part of Luke Ramsey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.000
appearing on five episodes of the witchy&nbsp;
Coven storyline. The son of the Christian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.620
Joan Ramsey — played by Patti LuPone — who&nbsp;
lives next door to Miss Robichaux's Academy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:48.540
Luke mixes in with the witches studying and&nbsp;
living there. However, his religious beliefs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:53.220
cause him a great deal of inner turmoil. In the&nbsp;
end — after getting literally stabbed in the back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:57.360
shot through the head, and put into a&nbsp;
coma — Luke is murdered by his mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:00.720
which follows his realization&nbsp;
that she killed Luke's father.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.120
"God told me you put the bees in the car.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.680
You knew dad was allergic to bees.&nbsp;
You knew you'd get away with it"

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:12.240
The role of Luke Ramsey introduced a&nbsp;
clean-shaven Dreymon to American audiences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:16.620
and made it abundantly clear that the actor&nbsp;
had both the talent and charisma to continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:21.240
his ascent into becoming a leading man for&nbsp;
any sized screen. It wasn't long after his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.440
American Horror Story debut that Dreymon really&nbsp;
began exploring the world of feature films.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.580
One year before he was cast in the leading&nbsp;
role of Uhtred on The Last Kingdom, and one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:34.380
year following his turn on American Horror Story,&nbsp;
Dreymon starred in the vampire romance thriller,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:39.180
Blood Ransom. He played the part of Jeremiah,&nbsp;
heading up a cast that also included Clifton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:43.920
Powell, Jamie Harris, and Emily Skinner.&nbsp;
Dreymon seemingly proved his ability to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:47.400
hold an entire production on his ample&nbsp;
shoulders, because it wasn't long after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.246
Blood Ransom that he was snatched up&nbsp;
by the producers of The Last Kingdom.

00:02:51.246 --> 00:02:52.140
"Don't be afraid."

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.060
"I'm not."

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:01.290
While Dreymon continued to demonstrate his range&nbsp;
by appearing in two more feature-length films —&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:07.500
the 2016 mystery Guys Reading Poems and the 2019&nbsp;
romantic crime-drama Heartlock – he was already an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:11.700
established name with a busy production schedule&nbsp;
thanks to the success of The Last Kingdom.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:16.260
Now, the future's looking bright for Dreymon,&nbsp;
who recently appeared in the Swedish thriller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:20.040
Horizon Line. The film also stars&nbsp;
Get Out actress Allison Williams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:24.240
with whom, in reality, Dreymon shares&nbsp;
a son and is romantically engaged.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:28.680
As Uhtred is fond of reminding us,&nbsp;
"destiny is all," and it certainly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.440
seems like Dreymon was destined&nbsp;
for stardom from the beginning.

